// quantum — Quantum computing with linear types and epistemic uncertainty
//
// The no-cloning theorem enforced at compile time via linear types:
// a Qubit must be consumed exactly once. Includes VQE simulation
// with GUM-compliant uncertainty propagation through gate angles.
// Classical statevector simulation; not a quantum computer.
//
// Submodules:
//   linear        — Linear Qubit type, gates (H, X, Y, Z, S, T, Rx, Ry, Rz,
//                   CNOT, CZ, SWAP, Toffoli), measure_qubit, Bell, GHZ3, teleport;
//                   simulator cap 10 qubits
//   vqe           — Variational Quantum Eigensolver with Pauli Hamiltonians and ansatz circuits
//   epistemic_vqe — VQE with gate-angle uncertainty propagation (statevector simulation)

// linear — types: Qubit (linear), QuantumState, QubitPair, QubitTriple,
//   MeasurementResult, TeleportResult, StateInfo
// Constants: QUANTUM_MAX_QUBITS = 10, QUANTUM_MAX_AMPLITUDES = 1024
//   (11th qubit_alloc panics)
// Key fns: quantum_state_new, qubit_alloc,
//   hadamard, pauli_x, pauli_y, pauli_z, s_gate, t_gate, rx, ry, rz,
//   cnot, cz, swap, ccnot,
//   measure_qubit (not `measure`: that name is the builtin Knowledge constructor),
//   bell_pair, ghz3, teleport, quantum_state_info,
//   amp_real, amp_imag, amp_prob
// Rx/Ry/Rz also exist on Statevector in epistemic_vqe; the simulators are not unified.

// vqe — types: PauliString, Hamiltonian, Gate, Circuit, CircuitState, CircuitVQEResult
// Key fns: pauli_string, hamiltonian_new, hamiltonian_add, h2_pauli_hamiltonian,
//   hamiltonian_expectation, hamiltonian_ground_energy (exact, Jacobi),
//   hardware_efficient, circuit_run, vqe_minimize (Rotosolve); <= 4 qubits

// epistemic_vqe — types: Statevector, VQEResult, GumBand, McBand
// Key fns: sv_zero, sv_apply_rx, sv_apply_ry, sv_apply_rz, sv_apply_h, sv_apply_cx,
//   h2_hamiltonian, h2_exact_ground_energy, vqe_optimize (Rotosolve),
//   vqe_gradient / vqe_hessian (parameter shift), vqe_gum2 (second-order GUM),
//   vqe_mc_band (Monte Carlo), vqe_epistemic
//
// Limits: linear statevector <= 10 qubits; VQE modules <= 4 qubits; no noise
// model, no shot noise, no hardware backend. Demo and cross-check: demos/quantum/.
